WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.759
Summer's almost here, which means blockbuster
season is kicking into gear.

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:09.960
The month of May saw new trailers for upcoming
superhero films, hard-rocking biopics, heart-pounding

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.459
horror flicks, and everything in between.

00:00:12.459 --> 00:00:18.050
In fact, we're already getting trailers for
movies coming out as far away as November,

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.320
so hold on tight, this is going to be a wild
ride.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.640
Here are all the trailers released in May
2018 that are sure to blow you away.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.189
Upgrade

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:33.260
Each new trailer for Upgrade raises the stakes,
making this look like one of the most unique

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.380
surprises of 2018.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.730
Logan Marshall-Green stars as Grey Trace,
a technophobe in the near-future who's implanted

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:44.830
with a computer chip that turns him into a
supercharged fighting machine.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.380
Early critic screenings have come out largely
positive, with the general consensus being

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.570
that Upgrade is a fun, action-packed, and
supremely violent movie, perfect for kicking

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.900
off the summer blockbuster season.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.600
With Leigh Whannell, creator of horror franchises
Saw and Insidious, pulling writing and directing

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.840
duties on Upgrade, you can count on a double
dose of insanity.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.380
Look for it in theaters on June 1st.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.869
Sicario: Day of the Soldado

00:01:10.869 --> 00:01:16.770
Josh Brolin and Benicio del Toro are back
in the latest trailer for Sicario: Day of

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:22.070
the Soldado, reprising their roles from 2015's
surprise gangland hit.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:26.659
This time, they're working to create a cartel
war in Mexico, using every means at their

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:29.759
disposal to escalate the violence and murders.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:34.979
Judging by the trailer, it's bound to be everything
that made the first one great and then some.

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:40.090
Sicario: Day of the Soldado is set to premiere
in theaters on June 29th.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:41.689
Escape Plan 2

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:46.350
There won't be a theatrical release for Escape
Plan 2, but that doesn't mean it's skimping

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.990
on the action, or the star power.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.929
Sylvester Stallone returns as Ray Breslin,
who was wrongly imprisoned in the first Escape

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:54.939
Plan.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:59.420
This time, he's putting himself behind bars
on purpose so that he can break out a prisoner

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.009
holding onto some sensitive information.

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:06.790
It's a race against time to find the valuable
prisoner before assassins can take him out,

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.750
and then it's a race against even less time
to get out of the prison alive.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.720
Dave Bautista joins the crew, and 50 Cent
is returning as well.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.140
You can check it out when Escape Plan 2 hits
Blu-ray and on-demand on June 29th.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.780
Ant-Man and the Wasp

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.990
More than perhaps any other Marvel property,
Ant-Man thrives on its fantastic visuals,

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.110
and the latest trailer for Ant-Man and the
Wasp promises so much size-swapping it'll

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.750
make your head spin.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.920
Most exciting though is the introduction of
the film's villain, Ghost.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.750
Originally introduced in the comic pages as
an enemy of Iron Man, Ghost is an anti-corporate

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:45.870
anarchist who uses a high-tech suit to pass
through solid matter.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.970
That extra element is bound to lead to some
insane fight sequences.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.750
Look for Ant-Man and the Wasp in theaters
on July 6th.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.380
Bleeding Steel

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.870
Jackie Chan is back in action with this summer's
Bleeding Steel, a sci-fi wonderland populated

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.280
by fancy headgear, colorful lights, and skintight
leather.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.250
Okay, so the trailer leaves a lot to be desired,
but it showcases some interesting concepts

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.020
and, of course, Jackie Chan kicking people.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.400
So many people.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.870
Bleeding Steel is going straight to video
on demand, and there are probably worse ways

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.600
to spend an evening at home.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.000
Look for it on July 6th.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.580
Skyscraper

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.460
In case you still weren't sure what Skyscraper
is about, the latest trailer lays it out pretty

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.460
clearly.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.270
Former FBI agent Will Sawyer lost his leg
in an explosion, and now he examines buildings

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.660
for a living to see if they have any security
flaws.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:41.900
While he's in China consulting for the world's
new tallest building, terrorists attack the

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.190
building and frame him for the job.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:48.420
Since his family's inside, he has to escape
the police and get inside.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:56.240
Don't worry, he makes it, and takes out the
terrorists one by one.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.400
Sounds like fun.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.360
Dwayne Johnson and director Rawson Marshall
Thurber previously collaborated on Central

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:07.060
Intelligence, and this newest team-up hits
theaters on July 13th.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.130
The Death of Superman

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:14.430
Say what you want about the DCEU, but DC runs
the game on animated films, and The Death

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.180
of Superman looks like a great new addition
to the animated line.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.319
This adaptation of the iconic 1990s crossover
event sees Superman facing off against the

00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:28.539
bloodthirsty monster Doomsday in an fight
that may just see the end of the Kryptonian

00:04:28.539 --> 00:04:29.539
superhero.

00:04:29.539 --> 00:04:34.050
And if you're thinking, "Haven't I seen this
cartoon before?" you're absolutely right!

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:39.990
DC's 2007 animated film Superman: Doomsday
was a lackluster attempt to combine all three

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.590
parts of the comic arc into one film.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:47.120
The upcoming Death of Superman is slated to
be the first in a two-parter, allowing more

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.250
of the story to unfold on-screen.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.240
Look for it on July 24th.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.169
Mission: Impossible - Fallout

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:59.069
Despite multiple sequels, the Mission: Impossible
franchise has never failed to disappoint.

00:04:59.069 --> 00:05:00.760
Well, after the second one at least.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.509
In the latest trailer for Mission: Impossible
- Fallout, we learn that, once again, the

00:05:14.509 --> 00:05:18.310
government doesn't trust Ethan Hunt to get
an important job done.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.490
Forced to go rogue, Hunt and his loyal team
have to track down a nuclear weapon while

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:28.699
staying two steps ahead of the CIA and their
superspy August Walker, played by Henry Cavill.

00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:33.340
The stakes are just as high as ever, the stunts
are just as real, and the mission is just

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.729
as impossible.

00:05:34.729 --> 00:05:39.659
Check out Mission: Impossible - Fallout when
it lands in theaters on July 27th.

00:05:39.659 --> 00:05:41.719
Mile 22

00:05:41.719 --> 00:05:46.409
Starring Mark Wahlberg, Mile 22 follows a
special forces operative who's tasked with

00:05:46.409 --> 00:05:51.800
protecting a police officer who knows the
location of nine pounds of missing radioactive

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:52.969
bomb material.

00:05:52.969 --> 00:05:57.490
The trailer builds up the initial premise
without giving too many details away, instead

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:03.159
focusing on Mark Wahlberg's gunslinging skills
and Iko Uwais' insane martial arts.

00:06:03.159 --> 00:06:07.620
The high-stakes action thrill ride is set
to hit theaters on August 3rd.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.860
The HappyTime Murders

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:14.530
If the Muppets were in a gangland drama written
by Sacha Baron Cohen and directed by Seth

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:20.469
Rogen, it might look a lot like The HappyTime
Murders, a raunchy, profanity-laden comedy

00:06:20.469 --> 00:06:23.520
about a world where puppets and humans live
together.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.020
When someone starts murdering a bunch of famous
puppets, two detectives embark on a journey

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.919
through the seedy underbelly of puppetville
to solve the case.

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:37.319
What's actually surprising about this is that
it's directed and co-produced by Jim Henson's

00:06:37.319 --> 00:06:42.379
son, Brian Henson, who previously directed
such family fare as The Muppet Christmas Carol

00:06:42.379 --> 00:06:43.800
and Muppet Treasure Island.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:47.919
The HappyTime Murders hits theaters on August
17th.

00:06:47.919 --> 00:06:48.919
Down a Dark Hall

00:06:48.919 --> 00:06:53.599
Uma Thurman is front and center in the new
trailer for Down a Dark Hall as headmaster

00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:58.259
of a creepy boarding school for girls where
something sinister may be lurking in the hallways

00:06:58.259 --> 00:06:59.259
at night.

00:06:59.259 --> 00:07:04.479
Based on a novel by Lois Duncan, Down a Dark
Hall follows troubled young Kit Gordy who's

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:09.500
transferred to Blackwood Boarding School and
finds herself face-to-face with a supernatural

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:10.500
threat.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:15.900
The trailer is heavy on the atmosphere, introducing
a faceless cloaked man, creepy occult rituals,

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.000
and the implication there are definitely sinister
happenings going down.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.940
Take a look on August 17th.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.199
Papillon

00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:29.099
The story of a man who's wrongly convicted
of murder and sentenced to life in a brutal

00:07:29.099 --> 00:07:34.139
prison in French Guiana, Papillon focuses
on his harrowing escape from prison and his

00:07:34.139 --> 00:07:36.879
adventures in the tropics after he gets out.

00:07:36.879 --> 00:07:42.189
Starring Charlie Hunnam as Papillon and Rami
Malek as his fellow escapee, Papillon looks

00:07:42.189 --> 00:07:44.860
like it hits all the right beats for a remake.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:50.320
It has adventure, high-stakes prison escaping,
and a love story holding it all together.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:54.180
Papillon sails into theaters on August 24th.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.650
City of Lies

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:59.659
There's a lot to take in from the first trailer
for City of Lies.

00:07:59.659 --> 00:08:04.509
Twenty years after the murders of Tupac Shakur
and Biggie Smalls, a journalist tracks down

00:08:04.509 --> 00:08:09.090
the detective who was in charge of the case
- Russell Poole, played by Johnny Depp.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:15.259
As he digs deeper, he uncovers a twisted conspiracy
involving the LAPD and the local gangs, and

00:08:15.259 --> 00:08:19.691
he's quick to learn that when you open a scar
that's been closed for twenty years, blood

00:08:19.691 --> 00:08:21.440
is bound to flow.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:26.199
Depp is in top form as the jaded detective,
but it's Forest Whitaker who really shines

00:08:26.199 --> 00:08:29.009
in the trailer as journalist Jack Jackson.

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:33.209
Check out City of Lies when it hits theaters
on September 7th.

00:08:33.209 --> 00:08:34.930
The Predator

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:39.909
Shane Black's Predator film finally released
its first teaser, dropping the extraterrestrial

00:08:39.909 --> 00:08:42.610
hunter right in the suburbs of Middle America.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:47.649
The teaser doesn't give away many plot details,
leaving the big surprises for the film itself…

00:08:47.649 --> 00:08:49.550
or maybe just future trailers.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:54.340
The preview begins with a young boy playing
with some kind of alien transmitter device,

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.860
apparently calling the Predator to Earth.

00:08:56.860 --> 00:09:01.240
Then, we're introduced to Boyd Holbrook's
character, a soldier who saw the alien when

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.860
its ship crashed.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:07.649
The Predator was written by Shane Black and
Fred Dekker, who previously teamed up for

00:09:07.649 --> 00:09:10.209
1987's The Monster Squad.

00:09:10.209 --> 00:09:14.490
Look for The Predator in theaters on September
14th.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.490
Mowgli

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:21.000
Sure, we just saw a high-profile live-action
version of The Jungle Book in 2016, but it

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.750
never went in a direction quite like this.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:28.780
Don't expect any ditties about the Bear Necessities
in Mowgli, which promises a darker take on

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:31.100
the young boy's jungle upbringing.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:35.959
Motion capture legend Andy Serkis directs
the film and voices Baloo.

00:09:35.959 --> 00:09:40.281
Christian Bale, Benedict Cumberbatch, and
Cate Blanchett also lend their voices to the

00:09:40.281 --> 00:09:41.281
film.

00:09:41.281 --> 00:09:44.500
Mowgli arrives in theaters on October 19th.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.350
Bohemian Rhapsody

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:51.570
Mr. Robot finally finds somebody to love in
the first trailer for Bohemian Rhapsody, a

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.740
bio-pic about the iconic rock band Queen.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:59.790
Rami Malek is transformed as frontman Freddie
Mercury in the trailer, sporting the rocker's

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.819
legendary mustache and all his on-stage swagger.

00:10:03.819 --> 00:10:09.100
Bohemian Rhapsody traces the band's formation,
their rise to fame, and one of Mercury's final

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.540
performances at the 1985 Live Aid concert.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:17.930
Mike Myers is also slated to appear in the
film, along with Game of Thrones' Aidan Gillen.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:22.899
Production on the bio-pic has been notoriously
troubled, with original director Bryan Singer

00:10:22.899 --> 00:10:28.279
getting the boot in December 2017 after reports
of him clashing with Rami Malek.

00:10:28.279 --> 00:10:32.209
Dexter Fletcher was brought in to finish the
film and oversee post-production.

00:10:32.209 --> 00:10:36.569
Hopefully the onscreen drama doesn't suffer
due to the behind-the-scenes drama.

00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:41.339
You can find out when Bohemian Rhapsody premieres
on November 2nd.

00:10:41.339 --> 00:10:42.339
Robin Hood

00:10:42.339 --> 00:10:47.150
It'd be easy to call the upcoming Robin Hood
film a knock-off of the non-stop-insanity

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.269
style of movies like Kingsmen.

00:10:49.269 --> 00:10:54.560
But hey, if you get an action movie where
you can actually see the action, everybody

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.560
wins.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:11:00.630
Filled with slo-mo arrow fights and exploding
horse-drawn carts, Robin Hood definitely looks

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:05.480
like a cheesily overblown take on the story,
but there's no denying that it's a feast for

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.610
the eyes.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:12.040
Starring Taron Egerton, Jamie Foxx, and Ben
Mendelsohn, Robin Hood will follow the familiar

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:17.040
tale: disgusted with the corrupt government,
super archer Robin makes it his mission to

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.720
steal from the rich and give to the poor.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.850
Look for it in theaters on November 21st.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.529
The Sisters Brothers

00:11:24.529 --> 00:11:29.630
It's a fact: The world needs more good Westerns,
and it looks like The Sisters Brothers is

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.630
set to deliver.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.770
For starters, it has an amazing cast.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:39.319
John C. Reilly and Joaquin Phoenix star, with
Jake Gyllenhaal, Riz Ahmed, and Rutger Hauer

00:11:39.319 --> 00:11:40.319
co-starring.

00:11:40.319 --> 00:11:44.660
The story follows the infamous hitmen the
Sisters brothers who are hired to track down

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:50.230
a gold prospector who stole from a local crime
boss, kicking off a darkly comic adventure

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.420
in the old West.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:56.709
The trailer promises a hilarious journey anchored
by the chemistry between Phoenix and Reilly,

00:11:56.709 --> 00:11:59.610
who play the skilled yet dysfunctional brothers.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:04.850
With so much talent onboard, The Sisters Brothers
is definitely a movie to keep an eye on.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:08.290
You can find it in theaters sometime in fall
2018.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.480
Thanks for watching!

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.060
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.420
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

